<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Apple's privacy manifest. Required for App Store submission.

    THE ANSWERS HERE ARE UNUSUALLY SHORT, AND THAT IS THE PRODUCT RATHER THAN AN
    OVERSIGHT. This app has no analytics SDK, no crash-reporting SDK and no
    messaging SDK, so there is no third-party processor to declare — every one of
    those decisions is recorded in docs/integration/privacy-and-dpa.md, and the
    short answer here is what they add up to.

    NSPrivacyTracking is false and there are no tracking domains, because nothing
    in this app follows a resident anywhere. The correlation id is per request and
    is asserted never to become a stable device identifier
    (test/core/observability_test.dart).

    Data types collected: none *by this app for its own purposes*. A resident's
    details reach the LGU's own server because they are applying for a municipal
    service, which is the service being performed rather than collection by the
    app — but this is exactly the line Apple's reviewers read differently from
    engineers, so it must be reconciled with the Data Safety form and the privacy
    notice before submission, and the three must say the same thing.

    Required-reason APIs: declared for what the Flutter engine and the plugins in
    this build actually reach for. Reviewed at TAB 22 against the dependency list
    in docs/integration/security-decisions.md; re-review when a dependency is
    added, because a new one can introduce a reason without changing a line of
    Dart.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- Flutter and flutter_secure_storage read and write files in the
			     app container; the timestamp reason is the one Apple expects for
			     an app's own sandbox. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- The launch flag and the app-lock preference. Nothing about a
			     resident: the session itself lives in the Keychain. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Flutter's engine reports free disk space when deciding whether it
			     can write a cache. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>E174.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Timers and elapsed-time measurement in the engine. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
